00:16:41,220 --> 00:16:43,390
Damage Report

263
00:16:41,220 --> 00:16:43,390
Central Avenue  Statue commemorating nation's founding: destroyed

264
00:16:41,220 --> 00:16:43,390
and the statue commemorating 
the founding is destroyed.

265
00:16:43,810 --> 00:16:45,690
But we just put that up...

266
00:16:47,160 --> 00:16:49,810
What?! Snack Bar Jura's sign?!

267
00:16:49,810 --> 00:16:52,070
O-Okay, I get it! I'll talk to her!

268
00:16:52,270 --> 00:16:55,440
As the representative of this 
nation and as her friend,

269
00:16:55,440 --> 00:16:56,560
I'll be tough on her!

270
00:16:56,560 --> 00:17:00,370
And this damage report just came to me.

271
00:16:57,120 --> 00:17:00,370
Additional Damages

272
00:17:00,920 --> 00:17:03,250
Rigurd... are you angry?

273
00:17:03,250 --> 00:17:05,030
Certainly not.

274
00:17:18,480 --> 00:17:20,820
Milim, I need more nails.

275
00:17:28,680 --> 00:17:31,300
Jeez, she fell asleep again?

276
00:17:31,300 --> 00:17:32,820
Some Demon Lord.

277
00:17:33,310 --> 00:17:35,550
She's worn out after so much excitement.

278
00:17:35,550 --> 00:17:39,450
She saw many new things and 
met many new people today.

279
00:17:39,860 --> 00:17:41,590
What is she, a child?

280
00:17:41,590 --> 00:17:43,350
Let her be a child.

281
00:17:43,790 --> 00:17:48,210
The key to living a long life 
is to stay young at heart.

282
00:17:49,130 --> 00:17:53,960
She lives free, lets her emotions 
run wild, and hates boredom.

283
00:17:54,140 --> 00:17:56,890
You enjoy that type of lifestyle, do you not?

284
00:17:56,890 --> 00:18:00,310
Yeah, but I'm the leader of a nation now.

285
00:18:00,310 --> 00:18:03,100
Responsibility comes before freedom.

286
00:18:03,460 --> 00:18:06,220
You have matured so much, Great Rimuru.

287
00:18:06,640 --> 00:18:07,600
In that case...

288
00:18:07,980 --> 00:18:10,860
I hope you will do the responsible 
thing and fix my sign.

289
00:18:11,220 --> 00:18:12,960
But I wasn't the one who—

290
00:18:12,960 --> 00:18:15,960
You are the leader and the one 
in charge of Lady Milim, yes?

291
00:18:17,240 --> 00:18:18,860
Great Rimuru!

292
00:18:19,100 --> 00:18:20,780
You can do it!

293
00:18:21,410 --> 00:18:23,160
Oh, all right. Guess I'll do it.

294
00:18:23,160 --> 00:18:24,700
Yay!

295
00:18:28,690 --> 00:18:29,920
Snack Bar Jura.

296
00:18:28,790 --> 00:18:32,920
Jura

297
00:18:29,920 --> 00:18:31,180
That's not the title!

298
00:18:37,460 --> 00:18:38,930
Hey, you're drooling.

299
00:18:39,090 --> 00:18:44,890
Inside Rimuru's Stomach

300
00:18:41,590 --> 00:18:44,910
This is a sight I never thought I'd see.

301
00:18:45,430 --> 00:18:49,570
Lady Milim certainly is 
quite the free spirit.

302
00:18:50,020 --> 00:18:52,440
Imagine falling asleep and being 
carried home on piggyback...

303
00:18:53,780 --> 00:19:00,450
So even you, as a fellow Catastrophe, 
frown upon her foolish behavior?

304
00:19:00,620 --> 00:19:02,120
Of course I do!

305
00:19:02,120 --> 00:19:04,880
If I weren't trapped in here,

306
00:19:04,880 --> 00:19:07,410
I would rip her off of 
him and smack her awake,

307
00:19:07,800 --> 00:19:10,250
then I'd bring down my 
fist as I lectured her!

308
00:19:11,710 --> 00:19:15,140
"That's supposed to be <i>my</i> place!"

309
00:19:16,220 --> 00:19:16,920
...is what I'd say.

310
00:19:17,940 --> 00:19:21,380
You want... to be carried piggyback?

311
00:19:23,810 --> 00:19:26,060
It's a heartwarming display 
of friendship, is it not?

312
00:19:26,060 --> 00:19:27,460
It's surreal.

313
00:19:27,460 --> 00:19:29,690
Also, you'd crush him.

314
00:19:40,380 --> 00:19:44,360
Rimuru, you love this nation that much?

315
00:19:45,460 --> 00:19:48,370
Oh, you heard us?

316
00:19:49,610 --> 00:19:52,800
Well, I did build this 
nation from the ground up.

317
00:19:52,800 --> 00:19:55,380
All the people in this town 
are precious to me, too.

318
00:20:02,930 --> 00:20:04,420
Aren't you scared?

319
00:20:05,540 --> 00:20:08,390
To have so many people who 
are precious to you...

320
00:20:10,020 --> 00:20:13,900
If even one of those bonds were to be lost...

321
00:20:16,940 --> 00:20:18,680
I'd be scared.

322
00:20:22,290 --> 00:20:28,430
The most precious things are 
always small and far too fragile.

323
00:20:29,440 --> 00:20:31,290
You will regret it.

324
00:20:32,200 --> 00:20:34,750
You'll regret building all this.

325
00:20:36,490 --> 00:20:40,960
And when that time comes, 
you won't be yourself anymore.

326
00:20:41,780 --> 00:20:43,560
Go back to sleep.

327
00:20:44,270 --> 00:20:45,270
Just sleep.

328
00:22:27,810 --> 00:22:28,950
<i>The next morning,</i>

329
00:22:29,600 --> 00:22:31,880
<i>Milim wasn't in the guest room.</i>

330
00:22:32,950 --> 00:22:37,430
<i>The only thing we found was a silence that made 
everything up to yesterday seem like a lie.</i>

331
00:22:44,730 --> 00:22:46,630
I'd be scared.

332
00:22:47,480 --> 00:22:48,480
Yeah?

333
00:22:51,550 --> 00:22:54,770
She might never come back here...

334
00:22:54,770 --> 00:22:56,310
I'm back!

335
00:22:56,550 --> 00:22:57,890
Want some, Rimuru?

336
00:22:58,100 --> 00:22:58,980
They're freshly picked!

337
00:22:59,340 --> 00:23:00,850
Where'd you get those?!

338
00:23:01,470 --> 00:23:04,190
I got them for fixing the 
fence around the farm!

339
00:23:04,190 --> 00:23:05,860
I said I was sorry, too!

340
00:23:05,860 --> 00:23:09,940
After all that talk about losing 
bonds and precious things?!

341
00:23:09,940 --> 00:23:11,860
Huh? What are you talking about?

342
00:23:12,170 --> 00:23:16,540
I can't wait to see what fun 
things will happen today!

343
00:23:17,640 --> 00:23:19,740
Great Rimuru!

344
00:23:20,350 --> 00:23:23,150
<i>Looks like this storm isn't over yet.</i>

345
00:23:24,000 --> 00:23:41,020
Preview

346
00:23:27,450 --> 00:23:29,130
Rigurd... are you angry?

347
00:23:29,330 --> 00:23:30,970
Certainly not.

348
00:23:34,040 --> 00:23:35,980
Next time, "A Fruitful Autumn."

349
00:23:35,980 --> 00:23:38,520
Rigurd, you <i>are</i> angry, aren't you?!

